\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 Monte Carlo Option Pricer with Black-Scholes & the Greeks -
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\
A Python-based European option pricing engine that combines Monte Carlo simulation with the closed-form Black-Scholes model.\
Prices call and put options via 10000 simulated stock price trajectories using Geometric Brownian Motion, computes all of the option Greeks both analytically and numerically \
and performs sensitivity analysis across key market parameters.\
\
Built using stochastic calculus, risk-neutral pricing, the Black-Scholes framework, and finite difference methods.\
\
\
\

\f0\b\fs36 What It Does -
\f1\b0\fs28 \
\
- 
\f0\b Prices European call and put options
\f1\b0  using Monte Carlo simulation with 100,00+ paths, achieving pricing accuracy within 1% of theoretical values\
- 
\f0\b Computes all five Greeks
\f1\b0  (Delta, Gamma, Theta, Vega, Rho) via two  methods -\
- Derived closed-form Black-Scholes derivatives\
- Calculated \'93bump and revalue\'94 applied to Monte Carlo result\
- 
\f0\b Simulates stock price
\f1\b0  paths via Geometric Brownian Motion using It\'f4 SDE \
- 
\f0\b Runs sensitivity analysis
\f1\b0  across volatility, strike price, and risk-free rate for both calls and puts\
\

\f0\b \
